 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nPicture inline creation returns None instead of inline element\n\nWhen trying to create a new picture inline element using `new_pic_inline()`, the method returns `None` instead of the expected inline element object. This breaks any code that expects to work with the returned inline element.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.parts.story import StoryPart\n\n# Create a document and try to add an inline picture\ndoc = Document()\nstory_part = doc.part\n\n# This should return an inline element but returns None\ninline = story_part.new_pic_inline('image.png', width=100, height=200)\nprint(f\"Inline element: {inline}\")  # Expected: <CT_Inline object>, Actual: None\n\n# Any subsequent operations on the inline element will fail\nif inline is not None:\n    print(f\"Inline XML: {inline.xml}\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Cannot access inline XML - inline is None\")\n```\n\nThe method should return a properly constructed inline element that can be used for further operations, but instead it returns `None` making it impossible to work with the created picture element.\n</issue>\n",
